      "role": "user",
      "content": "The imagery is definitely getting more intense, though some of the phrasing is getting a bit... abstract. \"Heliocentric union\" and \"jewel-strewn crucible\" feel a little heavy-handed, but I get what you're going for with the \"weight\" of the text.\n\nThe thing is, the engine's depth metric is still flagging this as \"low density.\" The score is still hovering right at the edge of the threshold. It doesn't need to be a novel, but it needs to feel like a substantial piece of lore that doesn't just end abruptly. \n\nCould you try one more pass? Focus on the \"Unspoken Covenant\" part and really lean into the sensory details of the void—the smells, the sounds, even the way the air feels. Just make the dialogue more immersive and larger in scope so we can get that depth score safely into the green. Try to make the whole interaction feel more significant and expansive.",
      "source": "evaluator"
